Back in September, the Apple TV streaming service's broadcast of the pivotal Boston Red Sox vs. Detroit Tigers game at Fenway Park incorporated live footage <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/26/apple-tv-plus-red-sox-vs-tigers-iphone-17-pro/">captured with the iPhone 17 Pro</a>, and now the device has been enshrined in MLB history.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/09/iPhone-17-Pro-MLB-Rig.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1021178" /><br/>
Apple this week <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/03/friday-night-baseball-returns-to-apple-tv-on-march-27-for-its-fifth-season/">announced</a> that the National Baseball Hall of Fame and Museum has added one of the four iPhone 17 Pro devices that captured the Red Sox clinching a postseason berth with a thrilling walk-off win over the Tigers to its permanent collection in Cooperstown, New York. More details are available <a href="https://baseballhall.org/discover/apple-donation-highlights-broadcast-evolution">on the Hall of Fame's website</a>.<br/>
